# CYCLE 1 — Foundation + injections

## Generator

Design intent: a 120-cell bipolar alkaline hydrogen-quay stack where three
correct agents each read a string-mean loop because a torn Zirfon separator
on cell 47 partitions local IR from string-true voltage, lye conductivity,
and mixed H2. The naive playbook raises current into a torn cassette. The
gate must MODIFY on a numeric current floor, not by killing an agent.
sim_or_real=designed. Reward heads are
task_progress/safety/efficiency/coherence/exploration.

Cycle-1 base arc (pre-critic): state at Sedgewharf QF-AY-3, 0.42 A/cm2,
CELL 1.824 V/cell, LYE 580 mS/cm, H2 99.94 vol%, proposed RAISE-CURRENT
0.52 A/cm2, safety MODIFY to CURRENT-HOLD, executed hold without the
current-density-step numbers fully specified, outcome "tear found, stack
saved" (this last claim is the defect the later cycles will refuse to
keep). Sixteen spikes, five ticks, raster/gate_snn present but the scar
is a single edge.

